    text: ' Whatever the source, the same four steps bring it into service. Do them with one small input first; widen later.  The Sources page: events, mapped and unmapped counts and last-seen time for each source, with a shortcut to its unmapped events.  Connect. Give Keen access to the upstream service. Built-in adapters use credentials you save on the source; the API ingester builder uses reusable encrypted connections. Collect. In Admin → Sources & evidence mapping → Sources , define the server or account, then add the users, organisations, repositories, feeds or queries to read. For a custom API, configure and publish an ingester in the builder. Inspect. Run a small collection and open one event. Check its source, timestamp and payload look the way you expect. Map. On that event choose Create mapping from this event , pick the controls and preview the rule. A rule set to All collected events (any collection) applies across every input of the source.  Each input in the Sources list offers Add mapping rule , which opens the mapping editor with that source and input already selected.  Forgejo, as a worked example. Start with a User collection and your account login, an Organisation collection and its login, or a Feed collection and its URL. The token decides which repositories Keen can read. Forgejo setup lists the settings and lookback. ',
