    text: " In the rule editor, Apply this rule to previously collected evidence in the background is selected by default; review it before saving. Saving the definition and finishing the background job are separate events, and the job reports its own status. You can also run Apply saved rule to past evidence on a saved rule at any time.  Admin → Remap is the broader tool, with date, limit, source, system, action and outcome filters. By default it processes events with no mappings; Include already-mapped events adds new rule-based mappings to events already linked elsewhere. Adding mappings is a different operation from removing stale ones.  Going deeper: version conflicts and revision history If another administrator saved a newer configuration, reload it and reconcile the two versions before saving. Restore this rule's revision is available for a saved rule: its history starts at revision 1 for that rule, ignores edits to other rules, changes only the selected rule, keeps collection settings and other rules, and does not remap historical evidence. Deleting a definition keeps its historical mappings. ",
