    text: " Build the organisation chart  In ISMS → Organisation chart , create a node with a name, type, optional parent, users and description, and associate the relevant controls and clauses. Parents represent your hierarchy; zoom and reset help with larger charts. Keep roles and people distinct, so a personnel change does not erase what a role means.  The organisation chart renders the hierarchy of teams and roles; the table beneath links each node to people, controls and clauses.  Maintain the People directory  In People & vendors → People , record a name, optional e-mail and position, an optional Keen account and organisation role, the assets or devices used, and notes. A person does not need a login. Changing the account of someone who sits quizzes needs quiz.manage , because the account decides whose quiz rounds and results it reaches.  Select the person, then add assurance records: screening, training, policy acknowledgement and the like. Each record carries a category, requirement, status, completion and expiry dates, an authoritative source, an evidence link and notes. Review records as they near expiry; the screening or training itself happens through the responsible team or provider.  Connect suppliers to assets  In Vendors , record the supplier's name, description, website, contact and the assets it supplies. An asset has one supplying vendor, so assigning it to a new vendor moves the relationship; check the current supplier before saving. Supplier risks and evidence belong in the risk and evidence records.  Maintain the asset matrix  In ISMS → Asset matrix , enter the asset, its category and subcategory, a licence where applicable, the owner, the Register held by relationship, a description and the relevant controls and clauses. Category, subcategory and licence lists have their own forms. Ownership and organisational responsibility are different from who is currently using a device.  The asset detail page shows its relationships and changelog, and Sample into audit where available. People who can read the risk register also see a Risks tab listing the risks recorded against the asset, highest first, with each one's treatment, scores and owner. When equipment moves or a service retires, update the asset's risks, supplier and people together.  Record access responsibilities  The Access control matrix records a task or action, the service, managed hosting accounts, status, who approved it, the roles and notes. Add a hosting-account record first if needed, link the intended roles and note the approval basis. Compare the matrix with real upstream permissions during access reviews.  Grant and revoke access in the external service itself. The matrix records the intended access. Keep passwords and API keys in your secret store and out of these records. Application Configuration records document context in the same spirit. ",
