    book: 'Using Keen',
    url: 'using-measures.html#effectiveness',
    text: " Open ISMS → Effectiveness measures . The Summary names what is measured in one line; the Description explains how the value is calculated, where the numbers come from and which exclusions apply. Write it so that someone who did not design it can repeat it. Enter the pass condition: the Threshold operator, Target value and Unit , for example at least 95 % . Choose No target for qualitative measures. Choose the Expected source , the Keen evidence source that supplies the values, or Other. If another system will submit observations, choose a stable Metric key . Then enter the owner, frequency, notes and linked controls. Save the measure. In Record metric entry , select it and supply the observed numeric value, or a qualitative value or status, in the intended unit, with the period start and end and the source (type, title, URL or reference). The source type starts as the measure's expected source. Associate a source event UUID where appropriate. Keen compares each numeric value recorded in the measure's unit with the target and marks it Meets target or Outside target . Explain exceptional results in Notes. Save and inspect the measure's Metrics tab; check the dates, value and source before using the result in a conclusion. Use Visualisations to review the trend with source and date filters, and investigate gaps and changes across the whole audit period.  Each measure shows its latest value against the target and links to the metric entries behind it.  Example. “Critical vulnerabilities fixed within agreed time” could use the percentage of eligible findings resolved on time, with a target of 95%. The measure must define the denominator, the exclusions, the reporting period and the source. Before you read “No new findings” as good news, confirm the scan ran and covered the intended systems.  Going deeper: metric keys and automated ingestion A metric key must be unique and may use letters, digits, dot, underscore, colon and hyphen. Automated metric ingestion has its own endpoint and authentication; ask the administrator to validate one sample against the configured provider, key and period before enabling recurring submissions. ",
