    text: ' Precision in the definition is what makes the numbers comparable later. Say what is counted, over which period, with which exclusions, in which unit, and which threshold means success. Link the measure to the controls it helps assess.  Create the measure with its summary and description, plus owner, frequency, expected source, target value, unit and threshold operator. Give an automated measure a stable, unique metric key and use the same key in the submitting integration. Changing the display title is different from changing this identifier. Record each observation with its date, period, numeric value or qualitative result, unit and notes, and a source title, reference or event where available. Check the Metrics and Visualisations views with source and date filters, so you compare like periods and populations. Open an entry to inspect its source and notes. Correct a mistaken observation deliberately and use the changelog to understand corrections. Sample the measure and the relevant observations into an audit. The measure explains the test; the entries supply the results.  Example. A backup-restore measure might target at least 95% successful scheduled tests. A value of 95 needs a denominator and a period, such as 19 of 20 tests completed in September. “One restore exceeded the objective” belongs in the note that explains the result.  Understand automatically recorded zeros  For eligible measures, Keen can record a zero for a closed calendar month with no observations. These entries are labelled Automatically recorded zero . They say that nothing was recorded under that rule; they do not prove that nothing happened, and they are not evidence that data was delivered.  Going deeper: which measures qualify The rule covers monthly and required/as-required measures whose target is zero and whose operator permits zero (blank, equals or at-most). An existing observation for the period prevents an inferred zero. Establish incident and exception coverage through the relevant source evidence and check collection coverage before relying on these entries. ',
