    title: 'Choose the features available in Keen',
    book: 'Administering Keen',
    url: 'administrator-deployment.html#installation-features',
    text: ' Open Administration → Features to switch workspaces and tools on or off for the whole installation. Everything starts enabled, each switch saves immediately, and the status message confirms the change. Only administrators can change these settings.  Features: switch workspaces and subsections on or off for the whole installation; records and evidence are retained.  A parent switch controls its children. Turning off ISMS makes SWOT, Objectives, documents, assets and its other subsections unavailable; turning off Risk management also turns off the Mitigator, CIA assessments, the risk register, PESTLE(E) and Interested parties. Child preferences are kept and return when the parent is enabled again.  Use these switches to control availability. They apply to everyone, administrators included, and the API rejects operations that belong to a disabled feature. Nothing is deleted: data, relationships and audit retention protections stay, and existing references can still appear in other enabled tools. A switch does not create a confidentiality boundary between users or erase information already downloaded.  Going deeper: individual switches and their side effects Audits, scheduled audits and sampling into audits have separate switches. Event sampling controls the PDF sampling action and adding event evidence to an audit. Questions controls asking, replying and the question workspaces. A question also follows the switch for the record it concerns: while evidence browsing is off, questions about events cannot be opened, asked or answered, and they leave My questions until it is on again. Incident actions can be disabled independently. Controls, Clauses, Sources, evidence browsing, framework visualisations and the connections explorer can be hidden. Shared framework and reference data stays available where other enabled tools need it, and evidence collection continues while evidence browsing is off. The Visualisations switch hides visualisation tabs and keeps existing evidence and relationships. Quizzes sit under ISMS. While Quizzes is off, quiz pages and My quizzes are unavailable, rounds neither open nor close and quiz emails pause; results already recorded on effectiveness measures stay. Audit attendee reminders follow the Audits switch. Account security, sign-in, administration and the administrative audit trail always remain available. Scheduled audit creation and automatic effectiveness measurements pause while their features are disabled, and question notifications queued before Questions was disabled are skipped. A request or job already admitted can finish. Changes take effect on subsequent API requests; reload an open page to refresh its navigation. If another administrator changes the settings while you are editing, Keen rejects the stale save. The configuration keeps a revision and the administrator responsible for each change. ',
