    url: 'administrator-identity.html#security-notification-ip',
    text: " KEEN_SECURITY_TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS lists the real reverse-proxy addresses or CIDRs, including the UI nginx hop when applicable. With an empty value, Keen uses the socket address, which behind a proxy is the proxy itself. Configure the real proxy chain before relying on unfamiliar-IP alerts, trust only the hops you operate, and restrict direct access to the API.  Going deeper: how the forwarded address is chosen Keen walks X-Forwarded-For from right to left while the current hop is trusted, stopping at the first untrusted address. Proxies must append the actual connecting peer or overwrite the header at the public edge; avoid broad trust ranges that include untrusted clients. If Uvicorn rewrites client addresses, either use --no-proxy-headers and let Keen perform this check, or make Uvicorn's trusted-proxy configuration equally restrictive. IP history begins when the feature is deployed, so each account's first observed address triggers one alert once mail is configured. Addresses are normalised, including IPv4-mapped IPv6; concurrent logins from the same account and address enqueue one alert; known addresses remain until the account is deleted; VPN and network changes can legitimately trigger alerts. ",
