    url: 'administrator-frameworks.html#organisation-frameworks',
    text: ' Keen ships 94 framework catalogues, and most organisations use two or three. This chapter chooses which ones appear, maintains their controls, and explains where the catalogues and the risk library come from.  Frameworks used by your organisation: tick the catalogues to offer in workspace selectors and save.  In Administration → Frameworks , search catalogue names and descriptions, filter by region or Enabled only , and page through the cards. Tick the frameworks your organisation uses and choose an organisation default. Expand the bulk-selection controls when needed, then choose Save organisation selection . At least one framework must remain selected. The workspace catalogue, navigation and mapping selectors follow the saved selection.  Hiding a framework keeps its controls, audits, evidence and mapping rules; it changes visibility, nothing else. Rules that should stop mapping evidence must be disabled separately. Reload open pages to refresh navigation; an unavailable previous selection falls back to the organisation default.  Going deeper: limiting the choices from the environment Set KEEN_ENABLED_FRAMEWORKS=ISO27001:2022,KEEN-AF:1.0 in .env to limit the choices offered in Administration. Use exact slugs separated by commas; an empty value allows every framework and unknown slugs are reported in Administration. If an environment change excludes all saved choices, the available environment frameworks are used until another selection is saved. ',
