    text: 'Every source has its own short chapter with the settings, the inputs it collects and the mapping advice. Built-in adapters collect from supported services; the API ingester builder configures other HTTP services; Keen Agent and webhooks receive pushed evidence; Diary evidence records human observations. Keen Agent / OTLP Jenkins Loki Elasticsearch Amazon CloudWatch Logs Cloud vendor posture AWS Microsoft Entra ID and Azure Google Cloud Akamai Cloud (Linode) DigitalOcean Scaleway GitHub Forgejo Gitea GitLab Redmine RSS / Atom IMAP mail Taiga BookStack Google Workspace Incoming webhooks Diary evidence Custom API ingesters Risk Ledger The Sources tab opens by default. Expand Source catalogue and collection health there to review collection status or pause ingestion. Use Evidence mapping to create and manage rules.  Connecting a source is the same three moves every time: define the connection, add a collection, map the events. This chapter walks that path once; the source chapters above fill in the details for each service.  Connection A named server or account, with its endpoint and credentials. Collection One thing Keen fetches from the connection: a repository, a query, a feed, a project. Mapping rule Which events from a collection count as evidence, and for which controls or clauses. ',
