    text: " Expand Rule insights , above Browse existing mappings , to see how each rule has matched over the last 90 days. Each rule in the list carries a badge, and the panel lists the rules to review first: Stopped matching : the rule has gone without a match for more than twice its usual longest gap between matches, and more than an hour, while its source kept sending events. The events may have changed shape, so preview the rule against recent events. No recent matches : the rule recorded no matches in the window. The panel says whether its source sent events in that time. Source quiet : the rule and its source fell silent together. Source insights opens the source's own activity. A rule with fewer than three matches shows No baseline yet . Gaps are estimated from hourly counts of the events each rule matched. An event records each control once, under the most confident matching rule or, among equally confident rules, the first; a rule that shares a control with another rule can therefore match events without recording them, and the panel names the rule that records them. Pause beside a rule, or Pause rule in the panel, keeps the rule, its revision history and its existing mappings, and Keen stops checking new events against it. Resume asks whether to check the events already collected as well, including those that arrived while the rule was paused; that runs the same background job as Apply saved rule to past evidence . Keen never pauses, merges or deletes a rule itself.  Going deeper: consolidation suggestions The panel compares the active rules with each other: Same conditions and controls : copies of one rule. The rule named already records the same evidence. Covered by a broader rule : every event the narrower rule matches also matches a broader rule, which maps all of its controls with at least its confidence. Same conditions, different controls : one rule can map all of their controls; choose one confidence where theirs differ. Same controls, different conditions : rules on one source that map the same controls. Where they differ in a single condition, such as the activity, the result or a pattern, the panel shows one pattern that matches exactly what those rules match between them: \\A(?:login|logout)\\Z for the activities login and logout , for example. Enter it as that condition's pattern under More filters in one rule, clear the exact value, preview the rule, then pause the others. Exact values of labels and payload fields stay exact, since a pattern stops on very long input where an exact comparison does not. Rules that matched the same events pairs rules whose conditions differ where at least 80% of the less active rule's matches, and at least ten events, were also matched by the other rule. ",
