    text: " Stable organisation and resource IDs prevent duplicate native records. Imports create missing vendors, supplier-service assets, risks, controls and domain links; existing local fields remain as edited. Changed upstream records produce additional evidence snapshots, absence upstream leaves local records and earlier evidence retained, and a deleted local imported record is recreated on a later enabled import.  Review imported ratings. Risk Ledger scores, impact, likelihood, owner names and numeric status are retained in snapshot fields and initial risk notes. Assign Keen ratings, owner and treatment state explicitly; its 5×5 scales and account identities have their own meanings, and no user accounts or People entries are created from upstream names.  Going deeper: names, controls and links Vendor names are never used to merge unrelated records; a name collision receives a stable Risk Ledger suffix. Risks without an available imported supplier use an organisation/supplier context asset without inventing a vendor record. A risk's explicit control association creates a native risk/control link when that control is imported. Controls use their upstream UUID as the stable reference. The title includes the domain letter and control number where supplied, the description retains the full question and guidance, and domain clauses group related controls. Imported control text is customer-fetched content, with source links retained. ",
