    text: ' Keen Agent is a small service that sends signed evidence to Keen: recognised activity from server logs and, on workstations, measured security settings. Getting one running takes three steps: register it in Keen, install and enrol the agent with a single-use code, and confirm the first evidence arrives. Everything else in this chapter is detail for when you need it.  Agent identity One registered collector. A Keen Agent proves it is that identity with its own key pair; Keen keeps only the public key. Enrolment code A single-use code, valid for 24 hours, that binds a new agent\'s key to a registered identity. Enrollment profile A bootstrap key that lets an autoscaling fleet register its own agents. Evidence envelope One Universal Evidence Utility (UEU) record: a typed, signed description of something observed or something that happened. Evidence mode How much of a server\'s log collection becomes evidence: recognised events only, events with their source lines, or every line. Source One log file pattern or journal selection on a server, with a parser that recognises its events.  The agent seals each envelope into a hash chain, signs each batch, encrypts each request to Keen and signs it, and Keen checks every signature, envelope and chain position before storing evidence; the agent trusts only an acknowledgement encrypted with the request\'s one-time key. Diagram source (Mermaid) flowchart TB\n  L["Logs, journal or posture probes"] --> P["Recognise, minimise and redact"]\n  P --> Q["Seal envelope: evidence ID, hash chain and checkpoint in one local transaction"]\n  Q --> T["Sign batch manifest and request; send OTLP JSON over verified HTTPS"]\n  T --> A{"Request signed by the agent\'s current key?"}\n  A -->|Yes| V{"Envelopes canonical, valid for their catalogue and listed in the signed manifest?"}\n  V -->|Yes| D{"Evidence ID already stored?"}\n  D -->|Same hash| OK["Return success"]\n  D -->|New| S["Record chain position, redact with custody record, store artifact and event; commit"]\n  S --> OK\n  OK --> R["Remove acknowledged envelopes from the queue"]\n  A -->|No| H["Pause delivery; retain envelopes"]\n  V -->|No| H\n  D -->|Different hash| H\n  T -->|Network error or retryable response| B["Back off and retry the same envelopes"]\n  B --> T  The agent is a standalone Go service for Linux, Windows and macOS. On servers it recognises package changes, authentications, privileged commands, denied access and security alerts in selected logs. On workstations a native companion measures disk encryption, screen locking, antivirus, firewall and automatic updates. Each item becomes a UEU envelope named by an event type from an event catalogue, and Keen checks it against that catalogue, renders it and applies the existing mapping rules. ',
