    text: ' On Windows and macOS, install the signed desktop package from keen.cloud/agent . Register the device in Keen as a Workstation linked to its person, then paste the enrolment code into the setup window that opens after installation. The setup helper enrols the native posture companion, saves its identity where only the system service can read it and starts it. On Linux workstations, install the server package and enable its posture collection as described in the agent repository.  Each run measures the five checks and sends one observation per measured setting and scope, followed by a coverage record listing the checks it attempted, measured and could not measure. Settings that cannot be measured are reported as unavailable; they never become evidence of a passing or failing state. Local account identifiers become pseudonymous subjects before they leave the device.  People pages show the result for each device. Keen judges the observations with versioned rules, and the result names that version. To apply your own policy, create effectiveness measures with these metric keys:  Metric key Unit Applies to keen.workstation.screen_lock_seconds seconds The longest permitted idle time before the screen locks, for example lte 900 . keen.workstation.antivirus_signature_age_days days The oldest permitted antivirus signatures, for example lte 3 .  With a target set, a configured screen lock or antivirus product meets the check only when its measured value satisfies the target; the observation shows both. A measure whose unit differs is ignored, and without a measure a configured protection meets the check. ',
