    title: 'Configuration and log semantics',
    book: 'Administering Keen',
    url: 'administrator-agents.html#agent-configuration-and-log-semantics',
    text: " examples/config.yaml holds the complete configuration with commented source examples. Each source names a path pattern or journal selection and a parser. Parsing is deliberately conservative: only records a parser recognises become events.  Parser Recognised events dpkg , apt , dnf software.package.changed : package installs, upgrades, removals and transactions, with versions and the requesting account as a pseudonymous subject syslog user.authenticated for SSH logins and failures, privileged.action.completed for sudo commands auditd Authentication and login records, privileged commands and denied system calls ( access.denied ) ossec security.alert.generated with rule, level, groups and description raw , json , nginx , php Lines only, in all_lines mode  Each source's evidence_mode (or the global default) chooses what it sends:  Mode Sends events Recognised events with typed attributes. The source line is represented by its SHA-256 hash and a file offset or journal cursor. events_with_lines Recognised events with their redacted source line included. all_lines Recognised events with their lines, and every other line as log.line.collected .  The identity's evidence mode limit in Keen is the most it accepts. An agent learns the limit when it enrols or renews its key and sends no more than it allows; Keen also enforces the limit on receipt. Above the limit, Keen removes an event's included line and records the removal in its custody record, and keeps no log.line.collected envelopes, while still recording their place in the agent's chain.  Choose paths carefully. Source paths are restricted to /var/log , a newly discovered file starts at byte zero, and a journal source's initial read uses initial_lookback , so a broad pattern can import an unintended archive. Unknown YAML keys and unknown parsers are rejected.  Going deeper: file safety, grouping and timestamps Configuration must be non-writable by group and others, credential files must also deny all access to others, and symlinks in any path component and non-regular files are refused. Keep log directories and configuration owned by trusted administrators. Dpkg and legacy syslog times use the agent host's timezone. Auditd records are grouped across reads and restarts, with interleaved IDs supported; an EOE record closes a group, and groups also close after three seconds without a new record or at the size limit. Hex-encoded audit EXECVE/PROCTITLE values remain encoded. multiline_start groups file records until the next matching line or idle/size boundary. Journald uses its native message boundaries and durable cursors; auditd grouping and multiline options apply to file sources. ",
