    title: 'Agent health and journal evidence',
    book: 'Administering Keen',
    url: 'administrator-agents.html#agent-013',
    text: " Agent heartbeats report delivery counters, queue size, source health, the agent's chain position, each source's evidence mode and whether a source asks for more than the identity's limit allows. Review these in the agent inventory to identify collection failures or delivery backlogs, and use the agent's local status and service logs to investigate a reported problem. Heartbeats also report, per source, how many lines were filtered out and how many were read but not recognised as evidence in the chosen mode.  Journal entries are recognised by their message: SSH authentication results become user.authenticated and sudo commands privileged.action.completed , with the account as a pseudonymous subject. In all_lines mode, other entries become log.line.collected with the redacted line and their service, process, priority and host attributes. Inspect an event's structured fields when choosing mapping conditions. ",
