    title: 'Filter before agent delivery',
    book: 'Administering Keen',
    url: 'administrator-agents.html#structured-agent-filtering',
    text: ' Filtering on the host keeps noisy logs out of Keen altogether. Each source accepts include_when and exclude_when lists, and each condition has a field (a literal parsed field key), an operator and a value .  Operators Notes equals , starts_with , contains , exists , in_cidr Quote numeric values such as "404" . Missing fields do not match.  By default each list uses OR: a record must match any include condition if any are given, and is then discarded on any exclusion match. Set exclude_match: all under the source to require every exclude_when condition (AND); for example, client.ip in 192.0.2.0/24 AND status equals "200" discards only status 200 requests from that network. Include conditions remain OR, empty exclusion lists discard nothing, and a missing field prevents an AND exclusion.  Going deeper: what filtering changes Redaction precedes structured filtering. Excluded records advance checkpoints but never enter the queue, and already queued events are unaffected. Status and heartbeats report persistent filtered_by_source counters for structured filters, separately from rejected records; raw regex filters are not included in those counters. Keep checkpoints when adjusting collection filters. ',
