    url: 'developer-architecture.html#1-architecture-and-repository-map',
    text: ' Keen is a FastAPI application over PostgreSQL, with Celery workers for collection and maintenance, Valkey for sessions and queues, and a static ES-module UI. This chapter maps the repository, follows one request through it, and sets out the conventions and checks a change is expected to meet.  The API uses SQLAlchemy models and Alembic migrations over PostgreSQL. Celery worker and beat use Valkey as broker and backend; Valkey also stores sessions, authorisation versions, caches and notification messages. The UI uses HTML, ES modules, Bootstrap and D3 with shared MOSP design-system helpers.  Where What lives there services/api/app/main.py Application construction, middleware and startup hooks. api/routes/ HTTP adapters; __init__.py assembles the domain routers. db/models.py , db/session.py ORM models; engine, SessionLocal and the request database dependency. Schema history is in services/api/alembic/versions . core/config.py , core/managed_configuration.py Environment settings; database-managed configuration. security/ Authentication, sessions, OIDC, roles, permissions, CSRF, rich-text sanitisation and redaction. ingest/ , mapping/ Source adapters with shared persistence and SSRF helpers; collection identity and rule evaluation. services/ , worker/ , storage/s3.py Domain operations, changelogs, statistics and scheduling; the Celery application and tasks; artefact storage. services/ui/public HTML pages and their pages/*.js controllers. app.js wraps and re-exports the MOSP helpers.  Going deeper: the UI build The UI Docker build installs the public design-system npm dependency at the commit pinned in package.json and its lockfile, applies the bundled compatibility patch and builds its assets. Keep the pin, lockfile and patch compatible with the application. ',
